now an hour or  so at least that i remember  during which a number of requests were  made by alex jones counsel of the judge  when it came to that digital copy and i  don't i didn't fully grasp the the sort  of fundamentals of what it was that they  were asking for on the basis that those  doc that that record was accidentally  sent to you what was it that they were  asking for and why was it that it was  not uh granted by the judge  well it's it's funny that you say you  were having trouble figuring out what  they were asking for because so were we  okay we uh  they were asking for things that made no  sense in the context they wanted the  judge to just do a blanket sealing order  over the entire documents but they had  no basis to just suddenly seal 2.3  gigabytes of information that's not how  these rules work okay they actually had  10 days from the time of disclosure to  specifically identify any documents that  either had a legal privilege like they  were between attorney they were husband  and wife something like that or that  were confidential because they were a  trade secret or sensitive in some way  and they just didn't do it um and so  when they came into the court having  violated all the rules to do that and  then were essentially saying that that  my side had somehow acted improperly  that was quickly dismissed by the judge  she actually did give them an  opportunity to in a day  designate anything as confidential which  means that i could still have it i just  couldn't share it outside the courtroom  they actually didn't do any of that um  so the second day of those hearings the  last day of trial basically the judge  declared them free and clear they're in  my hands now is going to become some bad  news for mr jones could mr jones argue  against the ultimate judgment on the  basis that his council inadequately  represented him  interestingly no you have that option in  criminal law okay if your criminal  defense lawyer provides you an effective  assistance that is a basis for appeal  but in civil law it is not and i think  it's a good rule because i think it'd be  rare that a criminal lawyer would  intentionally throw a case because this  client's going to end up in jail but in  a civil case it could it's more  foreseeable and so we don't let  ineffective assistance be the basis of  their defense particularly in criminal  law a lot of people have appointed  counsel they can't choose who their  lawyer is mr jones got to choose this  lawyer you revealed on the young turks  last week when speaking to our friend  anna casparian that in that digital copy  there was a nude photo of alex jones  wife sent to roger stone and since then  erica wolf jones came out and said  that it was non-consensual it's not  clear to me whether she means that the  picture was taken non-consensually or  she knew about the picture but it was  not consensual to send it to roger stone  what on earth is going on when it comes  to this this is almost like a side story  but raising a ton of different questions  about the relationship between jones and  stone and just bizarre things that you  often just never even see become part of  a trial is there anything else on that  that you've since found out  i mean the only thing that i can say  that i can help clarify the record on  that is because jones is actually what i  found was interesting is after i  discussed that jones actually showed the  picture on his show  which i thought was strange um but what  i can tell you is from the nature of the  picture it was definitely consensually  taken right it wasn't it wasn't  something that he was creep shotting her  or something like that uh the the  non-consent issue comes that it was sent  apropos of nothing to roger stone and  what seems to be a bid for his attention  that was totally ignored by stone uh  just a random picture that was sent in  some other messages trying to get his  attention  as terms of what's going on in the  future with those kinds of issues  because i brought that to the fore cause  it it does look like a crime and that's  not that's not an okay thing to do oh is  that right so it would be that even if  the picture was taken consensually to  disseminate it is potentially criminal  correct and i mean there's some there's  some caveats to that in texas there has  to be basically an intent to harm or  embarrass or something like that but  sending your wife's picture to roger  stone non-consensually pretty much meets  that that definition um and so you know  i'm glad that miss wolf jones knows  about that now um and and there's a lot  of other things in those text messages  that will likely come out in due course  which raise other troubling issues in mr  jones's life um and so as that process  goes forward uh there may very well be  more revelations about what's going on  there  uh do you think i might have a  defamation case against alex jones he  did call me a predator about six months  ago because i have a paid membership  program on my show where people can pay  and get access to an extra 20 minute  show a day i can't really say that i was  damaged by it in fact it was probably  the best possible thing that's ever  happened to be honest i probably don't  have a case right no i would figure not  for a couple reasons one is you're very  much a public figure now you know uh you  are a guy involved in the middle of the  discourse and in this country we let you  be pretty reckless right up to the edge  about public figures right different  than the sandy hook parents right um but  it's also funny that i just find it  ironic that here you are talking about a  promotion program you're doing on your  your show for more content right and  here's a guy who's hawking  you know super male vitality and brain  force and he's calling you a predator  that's that's really funny to me i i  think it's also funny you bring this up  because somebody was asking me today to  explain said can you who's david pac-man  what's the show about obviously an older  person is not watching their news on the  internet sure and the best thing i could  come up with was  imagine if alex jones wasn't bad  imagine if somebody was doing news and  commentary on the internet in an  independent way that wasn't just a grip  to try to sell you pills that turn you  red right like what if you had that and  and i'm you know that's one of the  reasons i went on tnt tyt one of the  reasons i was really happy to come here  yeah is because the solution sure isn't  good through the corporate media it's  through shows like this and by people  who are taking it seriously being  responsible well i appreciate that um  last thing i want to ask you about the  last time i was in the same room with  alex jones was years ago at a radio  conference called the new media seminar  which i don't even know if it exists  anymore and at the time my impressions  were he's playing a character my  impressions were that he got off the  stage after giving a sort of animated  but still kind of normal speech and he  said something like you know i could  have really freaked him out if i wanted  to and it seemed that he sort of  understood that the on-air persona was  not at all his sort of real life in the  last two years from everything i've seen  and read in interactions with jones out  in public that people have it's  increasingly seeming like the the  infowars alex jones is the the real guy  in your experience having been in the  room with him for as long as you were is  it is it a character or is that the real  alex jones you know that is a question i  have struggled with since the beginning  and at the start i thought i knew the  answer and i think that has changed over  time for me it's you  you see at first i was positive and i  still remain very positive that most of  the things he said for instance about  sandy hook he never believed he never  believed there were pictures of the  children still alive he never really  believed the school was shut down and  stocked and was a fake school i don't  think he believed any of that and so  there was a time that i really believed  that he was a sophisticated operator  completely detached from the things he  was saying but as we went through this  whole process i deposed him several  times as we went through trial i also  realized there is no off switch for  jones and there is a something about  spending every day wrapped in your own  bs that it starts to actually affect you  and there is a mindset jones i think  you're right when you say that he is  conscious of how his words appear to  people he and he is any and he wants to  try to control that but here we just saw  him in this trial  totally unable to turn off the freak  flag just for 10 minutes in front of  that jury and it really shows that  there's there's two sides of jones  there's a very very conscious  manipulator side to jones and then there  is a side where he is not really in  control of himself those two parts of  himself are at war and right now the  part of him that's out of control has  been winning handily for the last couple  years yeah out of control is uh quite  quite an understatement uh mark bankston  partner at farah and ball and lead  counsel in a number of defamation  lawsuits against alex jones and infowars  mark really a pleasure having you on  today  hey really pleasure being here if you  ever have legal questions and want to  talk about some more stuff please have  me back
 

